      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "mobile-agent-summary",
      "description": "Mobile-only semantic role orientation immediately after the hero; hidden above 680px.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-mobile-agent-summary\" aria-label=\"Three agent roles and handoffs\"><dl><div><dt>Supply Chain Agent</dt><dd>Discover upstream risk</dd></div><div><dt>Remediation Agent</dt><dd>Propose the repair</dd></div><div><dt>Development Security Agent</dt><dd>Watch, test and verify</dd></div></dl><p>Supply Chain → DevSec baseline → Remediation → DevSec replay → human review</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-mobile-agent-summary{display:none;font-family:var(--font-public,'Public Sans'),sans-serif}@media(max-width:680px){.ds-mobile-agent-summary{display:block;margin:0 0 23px;padding-bottom:18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#32352f)}.ds-mobile-agent-summary dl{margin:0}.ds-mobile-agent-summary dl>div{padding:9px 0}.ds-mobile-agent-summary dt{width:auto;padding:0;background:transparent;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink,#f1f1eb)}.ds-mobile-agent-summary dd{padding:0;font-size:10px;color:#bac7ac;margin:4px 0 0}.ds-mobile-agent-summary>p{font-size:10px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--green,#c7ef79);margin:11px 0 0;max-width:48ch}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Verification Interlock",
    "overview": "A patch moves only when its proof aligns. The user-selected dark engineering workspace gives the evidence workflow the character of a precise instrument: charcoal surfaces, warm white type, restrained lime and an isometric mechanism whose position carries meaning.\n\nThe workspace is compact and operational. Selected findings, before/after evidence and explicit verification states carry the hierarchy. Public Sans keeps interface copy direct; thin borders and small tonal shifts organize dense information. The machine provides the signature silhouette and makes the gate tangible.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Charcoal surfaces with a muted olive cast and warm white text.",
      "Restrained lime for primary action, selection and satisfied evidence gates.",
      "Compact evidence surfaces with explicit status and human review authority.",
      "Functional isometric geometry tied to the selected finding's state."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State Has Words Rule",
        "body": "Color reinforces a written verification state. A lime cartridge alone never asserts that a patch is verified.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Before Ornament Rule",
        "body": "Geometry must explain the selected finding's progression. Keep the machine's five gate fingers and cartridge movement tied to evidence state.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Baseline Before Candidate Rule",
        "body": "Supply Chain sends its risk brief to DevSec; DevSec records an affected baseline and freezes checks before Remediation writes. Remediation returns the candidate to DevSec. Local-change jobs enter through DevSec and request repair directly. Gate failure routes the failed evidence back to Remediation for another candidate; passing security checks never erase failed legitimate-use controls.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the charcoal, warm white and lime roles to extend this engineering workspace.",
      "Do show a written status next to every meaningful color or gauge result.",
      "Do preserve all five gate conditions and the blocked middle finger when regression fails.",
      "Do retain visible status and a reachable action in every mobile finding row.",
      "Do preserve synthetic labels, human review authority, visible focus and reduced motion.",
      "Do treat `workspace.css` and the current feature components as the built visual source.",
      "Do preserve exactly three product agents and identify controller, evidence, gate and human review separately.",
      "Do keep DevSec baseline/frozen checks before repair, candidate replay and failed-check return visible at both graph sizes.",
      "Do keep advisory snapshots, fictional inventory and simulated test results explicitly distinguishable.",
      "Do retain owner follow-up as a hold even when all five represented checks pass."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't describe simulated evidence, placeholder identifiers or local draft previews as live execution or a sent pull request.",
      "Don't advance the machine through a blocked gate or display five active gauge notches for four satisfied checks.",
      "Don't hide mobile status behind horizontal table discovery.",
      "Don't turn every panel into a floating shadow card or add decorative animation to verification states.",
      "Don't restore the earlier rejected concept from the root design specification.",
      "Don't present the deterministic controller as a fourth agent or grant an agent merge authority.",
      "Don't turn a ready graph state into an automatic merge or a guarantee of complete security."
    ]
  }
}
